    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d16">

                <pb facs="0095" n="11" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg11"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72114/2885</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-10-03T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 3, 1917, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>988. Your 1650, September 15, noon. Department is of the opinion that limit of
                    1,000 parcels transported by each steamer of the French Line will for the
                    present be an ample allowance and that no steps need yet be taken to ship by
                    other means the number of parcels in excess of quantity named.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
